WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.423
Sometimes the revolution is quiet.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.140
That's certainly the case with Formula E.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.830
Launched in 2014, it's an
all-electric racing circuit

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.340
that wants to capture the excitement

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.080
around one of the most
successful sports in the world:

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:17.913
Evans cuts across,

00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:20.150
and the crunch of carbon fiber.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.840
It's a plan that's at once obvious

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.530
and utterly audacious.

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.370
Sure, the world's accelerating
toward a greener future

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.910
spurred by the devastating
effects of climate change.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.880
But success for Formula
E means a tricky balance

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.400
of competing stakeholders.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.990
We're talking about automakers
eager for a new technology,

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.880
would-be customers for electric cars,

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.770
and of course, finicky fans.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.040
And some of them are quite
happy to keep watching faster,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.080
louder cars speed through
the world's greatest cities.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.510
The main power of sports
is the fact that it touches

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.283
the heart, the mind,
the souls of its fans.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.650
Definitely, transport sector
is one of the big areas

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.140
where the world needs
massively to improve.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.740
If you think about the 25

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.580
most watched television programs ever,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.860
24 were sport events.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.730
If you can use the power of
sport for a positive agenda,

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.013
that's really powerful.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.900
I'm here in Monaco, which
is known for lots of things,

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.010
especially things related to money.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.010
It's also really known for its role

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.440
in the world of motorsports, fast cars.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.610
In fact, the Monaco Grand Prix happens

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.325
on the streets just behind me.

00:01:39.325 --> 00:01:41.290
Monaco is a tiny country,

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.110
the world's second smallest, in fact,

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:44.810
trailing only the Vatican.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.289
It's tucked along the Riviera
between France and Italy.

00:01:47.289 --> 00:01:49.000
And when you think of Monaco,

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.120
the first things that come to mind

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.263
are probably James Bond movies
or the fast beautiful car.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.000
Its status as one of the world's
premier motor racing stages

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.470
came after World War II,

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.420
when Formula One races began
emerging through Europe.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.550
The sport quickly attracted

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.965
both drivers willing to
travel the world to race

00:02:05.965 --> 00:02:09.210
and a rabid fan base hoping
to witness the spectacle

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.540
in person or on TV.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:12.760
While Formula One racers

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.050
could initially buy and
race their own cars,

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:17.130
it also attracted major automakers

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:19.760
like Mercedes-Benz,
Alfa Romeo, and Maserati

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.370
to showcase their latest
and greatest motor tech.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.030
Tech like active suspension
and carbon brakes

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.210
that would eventually
distill down to cars we see

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.590
on the road today,

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.250
F1 also created legends
like Juan Manuel Fangio,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.600
Lewis Hamilton, and of
course, Michael Schumacher.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.630
Michael Schumacher

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.230
leads the world championship.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.250
Formula One's a huge
sport in Europe and Asia,

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.300
averaging more than
900,000 viewers per race.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.150
That's on par with some of the UFC fights

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.750
we see here in the States,

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.920
with the audience growing partly
due to an unlikely source:

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.480
Netflix.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.970
Formula One is the ultimate competition.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:55.920
"Drive to Survive,"

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.405
a series that documents the drama on

00:02:57.405 --> 00:02:59.620
and especially off the track

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.250
is one of the streamers' biggest hits

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.870
of the past several years.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.150
It's drawn in a whole
new generation of fans

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.540
tuning in and showing up to the races.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.310
Netflix are a real bunch
of [****] aren't they?

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.050
Every year, legendary racers

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.410
navigate the hairpin turns

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.760
in cities across the world

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.640
for throngs of fans perched
on rooftops and balconies,

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.920
just trying to catch a glimpse.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.240
And a few decades ago,

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.680
Alejandro Agag was a kid

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.360
watching from his parents'
apartment right here in Monaco.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.780
Oh yeah, that was the
first time I saw a race,

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.180
from the terrace of our apartment

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.460
where my parents were living.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:31.430
Previously, there was a Formula
One driver living there.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.263
No kidding.

00:03:32.263 --> 00:03:33.990
So they were, in the drawers
you would see some stickers

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.087
and some things

00:03:35.087 --> 00:03:38.743
and it was great to have that memory.

00:03:42.947 --> 00:03:45.620
Alejandro is the chairman of Formula E.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.210
Politician turned businessman,

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.600
he found his way to motorsport

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.980
and ultimately ran a team in 2007

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.270
in the second division of Formula One.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.060
He went on to recruit
sponsors to the circuit

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.983
and there he saw an opportunity.

00:03:59.945 --> 00:04:00.880
I was, at the time,

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.490
working around the Formula One business,

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:03.650
mainly with sponsors.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.820
In every email,

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.790
it had some kind of concern
about sustainability,

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:10.870
about carbon emissions.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:12.380
So that's kind of when I thought,

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.560
we should create a green version of it.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.830
Formula E is trying to ride and accelerate

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:20.780
a movement towards sustainability
that has urgently risen

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:21.920
in the past several years,

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.180
driven by young activists
like Greta Thunberg,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.610
part of a generation speaking out loudly

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.630
about the climate crisis.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:31.120
When I started my career 10 years ago,

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.100
sustainability was something
that was kind of trendy,

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.150
but not exactly, you know,

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.870
like the central priorities.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.630
Definitely, Formula E is much more

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.410
than a race that is putting cars on track,

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.220
but Formula E is really a
platform that is here to showcase

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.840
that a sustainable lifestyle,

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.190
that we are going to
be finding really cool,

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:50.850
really exciting.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.120
This is Julia Pallé,

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:55.563
she's the head of
sustainability for Formula E.

00:04:55.563 --> 00:04:57.680
To make sure the race
circuit and its teams

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.080
are living up to the big promise

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.380
of helping solve that global crisis.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.670
My mission is to make Formula E

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.031
the most sustainable sport possible.

00:05:05.031 --> 00:05:06.810
This has now been the
first sport in the world

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:08.870
to achieve net zero
carbon since inception,

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.431
phasing out of plastic onsite,

00:05:10.431 --> 00:05:12.990
offering vegetarian options to our fans,

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.500
trying to use less planes

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.560
to fly over our freight and so on.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.810
But how to go green

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.480
and who's leading the
charge has become tricky.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.870
Recently, big companies,

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:24.630
including those associated
directly with fossil fuels

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.570
and their consumption,

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.030
have seen the commercial value

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.070
of moving toward being more sustainable.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:31.370
Ford has pledged to invest $30 billion

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.990
in electric vehicles by 2025,

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:37.200
having just spent $11
billion this past September

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.160
on electric trucks and battery plants.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.240
Volkswagen is more than doubling that,

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.451
with the goal of investing $83 billion

00:05:43.451 --> 00:05:45.500
in the next four years.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:49.070
And their involvement has
made Alejandro's job trickier.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.060
Some people will not get involved because,

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.240
maybe they say that we're
doing this to look good.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.340
I think so many companies,
so many corporations,

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:56.435
would do more for the environment

00:05:56.435 --> 00:05:59.380
if they were not scared
of someone just coming

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.940
and calling them green washing.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:03.350
You have to include everyone
on the climate action.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:04.501
If you don't include everybody,

00:06:04.501 --> 00:06:06.199
including the big oil companies,

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:09.003
including the big energy
companies, including everyone,

00:06:09.003 --> 00:06:10.733
you will not succeed.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.260
That's especially challenging

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.650
when at least part of Formula E's success

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.360
relies on the investment
of the major car companies.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.300
The relationships there
have been important,

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.670
but thorny at times.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.080
The car companies very
much have a vested interest

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.490
in using the technologies of Formula E

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:30.313
and its teams are collectively
developing their cars.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:35.680
Motorsport is a sport where
the driver puts helmets,

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.410
puts specific gloves,

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:40.340
so we can take more risks

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:43.323
and test very ambitious technologies.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:45.553
This is Xavier Pinon,

00:06:45.553 --> 00:06:47.770
he's the technical director for FIA,

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:49.240
the governing body that sits across

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.772
both Formula One and Formula E.

00:06:51.772 --> 00:06:56.140
The voltage for the usual
EV car in the street,

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.623
it's something between
200, 300, 400 volts.

00:06:59.483 --> 00:07:02.420
In a Formula E car,
it's close to 1000 volt.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:05.310
For sure, we will not be
able to take this apart

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:07.433
from the racecar to put it on the road car

00:07:07.433 --> 00:07:10.140
but the technology
inside will be the same.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.557
Thanks to the motorsport,

00:07:11.557 --> 00:07:14.220
the car manufacturer can take more risks,

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.683
can accelerate the
research and development

00:07:16.683 --> 00:07:17.516
with the supplier.

00:07:17.516 --> 00:07:20.370
But keeping the manufacturers
engaged via teams

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:21.720
has proven elusive.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.930
Both BMW and Audi earlier this year

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:26.510
said they wouldn't field
teams in the upcoming season

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:28.740
claiming they have what they need for now,

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.150
from a technical perspective,

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:32.280
to help with their EV push.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.320
Alejandro?

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.240
He's unfazed.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.960
He said it was a natural circle of life

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.940
he'd seen before in motorsports.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:39.270
It happened in Formula One.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.320
We had a few manufacturers,
German manufacturers,

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:42.153
that came on board.

00:07:42.153 --> 00:07:43.630
The budget go up, and then they say,

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:44.700
"Oh, it's too expensive."

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:45.680
And they leave.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:46.790
For other car makers,

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:49.440
Formula E continues to be a valuable lab,

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.539
especially as EVs seek to make the jump

00:07:51.539 --> 00:07:54.290
from selling to affluent
customers in the west

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:56.030
to more emerging markets.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:58.523
The latter is where
Mahindra Group is focused.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:02.860
When we got into Formula E

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:03.693
we were really thrilled

00:08:03.693 --> 00:08:05.710
with the level of competition we got.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.240
We were now, for the first,

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:10.499
time having a platform to show
the quality of our product

00:08:10.499 --> 00:08:13.083
against what was perceived
the best in the world.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.740
There's no reason why a Mercedes or a BMW

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:21.460
in the Indian market should
command a 250% premium.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:24.263
This is Dilbagh Gill, he
runs Mahindra's racing team.

00:08:25.166 --> 00:08:27.220
He's a veteran of that Indian conglomerate

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:29.350
and deeply tied to sports in general,

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:31.530
and motorsports in particular.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:33.970
When the opportunity to run
the Formula E team came up

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:37.330
at a dinner almost a
decade ago, he volunteered.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:40.531
We were evaluating
motorsport platforms in 2012

00:08:40.531 --> 00:08:43.110
after some amount of success
with the motorcycle racing.

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:44.775
And when Formula E came to us,

00:08:44.775 --> 00:08:47.540
it sort of segwayed really
into what we were looking at

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:50.770
in the next 10 years in terms
of our mobility solution.

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:53.610
So we took a call to participate.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.170
I was with, I think Anand Mahindra

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:56.281
and a couple of other people

00:08:56.281 --> 00:08:59.027
at a dinner in Delhi, I just
raised my hand and said,

00:08:59.027 --> 00:09:01.650
can I have the opportunity
to run the team?

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.460
And yeah, sometimes you gotta
be careful what you wish for

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.293
because it comes true.

00:09:04.293 --> 00:09:06.730
And that came true that evening.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.420
Mahindra has a different market

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.280
in scale and potentially
in terms of difficulty.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.370
India's power grid is
notoriously underdeveloped

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:15.850
and unreliable.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:18.460
And the vehicle fleets
aren't just mid-sized sedans

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:21.000
and SUVs in many parts of that country,

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.640
but small vehicles called tuk-tuks.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.000
Interestingly today,

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.010
the largest selling product which we have

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:28.380
is electric tuk-tuks.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.670
We are selling, I think
maybe 5 - 6,000 per month

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:31.540
and it's only increasing.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:32.373
It's just that we can't keep up

00:09:32.373 --> 00:09:34.010
with the demand at this point in time.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.000
When you talk about pollution,

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.320
we are not only just talking
about smog and smoke,

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:38.940
but we need to talk about noise pollution.

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:41.300
Think of that loud exhaust
noise coming from a tuk-tuk,

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.380
which has started
accelerating down the street,

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:46.210
and now you have silent tuk-tuks
or a silent bus going by.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.923
It tremendously improves
the quality of life.

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:53.160
We did not join Formula E for technology.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.990
We joined Formula E because we
felt it was important for us

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:58.540
to be a partner in the
sustainability effort.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:01.006
So, Mahindra plays in
20 different industries.

00:10:01.006 --> 00:10:05.490
Our biggest industries
are auto, farm equipment,

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:08.090
we have a real estate business,
and a logistics business.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.750
We then have a solar business.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.400
We've got a company that
recycles automobiles,

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.290
and we've got a number of
other businesses around

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:18.270
aerospace, defense,
agriculture, and a few others.

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:20.200
They may have a huge slate of entities

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:23.340
in its roster, both Mahindra
and Formula E recognize

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:26.050
the power of sport in
cultures across the world

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:28.850
and its ability to influence change.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:31.470
You've seen this, as you say,
from different perspectives,

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:35.650
both at Michelin, and now being
part of the Formula E team,

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:39.690
what is it about sports and
sport that influences us,

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:40.523
do you think?

00:10:40.523 --> 00:10:42.310
I think the main power of sports

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:45.460
is the fact that it touches
literally the heart,

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:47.900
the mind, the souls of its fans.

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:49.790
Whatever is your sport

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:52.120
you're like a kid in
front of the athletes.

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:54.610
You're really gonna like
inspired by what they do,

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:56.150
what they achieve.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.240
It's a sport where you've got,

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:00.380
not only the focus on climate change,

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.400
but more importantly, it's a lot more fun

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.870
because the racing
happens in city centers.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:08.650
And that will also have
people start looking at EVs

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:09.483
in a different light

00:11:09.483 --> 00:11:12.910
and say that this is
a great option for us.

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:14.390
If you look at a per capita basis,

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.740
India is the world's
worst sporting nation.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.500
1.3 billion people and
we really don't have

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:20.940
much of record in sports so
I think through Mahindra,

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.360
through our various initiatives,

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.800
what we're trying to do is help people

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.971
to move from viewership to participation.

00:11:26.971 --> 00:11:29.134
And as a recovering politician,

00:11:29.134 --> 00:11:32.290
Alejandro also sees
Formula E as an engine for

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:34.490
political and social change.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.670
I just came back from Saudi Arabia

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.740
where I was scouting locations near Neom.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.490
And it used to be very closed,

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:42.323
very strict.

00:11:42.323 --> 00:11:43.156
Very closed, yeah.

00:11:43.156 --> 00:11:46.090
And of course, there's
still a long way to go,

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.787
but I think they're making good progress,

00:11:48.787 --> 00:11:50.333
especially with women.

00:11:50.333 --> 00:11:52.190
You know, now a woman
can drive, for example.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:55.970
Actually, Formula E was
really part of the change

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:57.030
in Saudi

00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:59.390
because we were the first event ever

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:01.840
where women and men non-related

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.060
were allowed to just
be together and dance.

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:05.030
I mean, we were really proud

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:06.830
to be able to be part of the change.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.080
For Alejandro,

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.130
Formula E is part of a broader portfolio

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.280
of electrification in sports.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:15.320
He also runs Extreme E,

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:17.080
that's an off-road racing series

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:19.290
that uses all electric vehicles.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:20.930
And the week we met in Monaco,

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.280
he was in town to take advantage

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.495
of another quintessential piece of Monaco:

00:12:24.495 --> 00:12:26.053
the boating industry.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.220
The Monaco yacht show was set to kick off,

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.310
and one evening Alejandro and his team

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.340
took over the Monaco yacht clubs' deck

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:39.260
to unveil an electric speed boat

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.980
that will race around that harbor,

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.810
and several other famous waterfronts,

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.490
starting in 2023.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.040
We launched the Racebird,

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:48.870
the electric power boat
that is going to be

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.240
the boat that is going to race

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:53.290
on the E One world championship,

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.920
electric power boat world championship.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.159
This project is starting
now all around the world,

00:12:58.159 --> 00:13:00.827
that's why it's the best moment
to create a championship,

00:13:00.827 --> 00:13:02.810
an electric power boat championship,

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.059
to serve as a platform for
the industry to kind of

00:13:05.059 --> 00:13:07.780
showcase what it's doing to decarbonize.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:12.320
You have to basically
move to electric mobility,

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:15.220
electric propulsion in every space.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:16.940
You have to move on the cars,

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:17.940
you have to move on the roads,

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.999
and you have to move on the sea.

00:13:19.999 --> 00:13:21.270
This is the boat.

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:22.810
You see the foils,

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:23.890
the propeller in the back,

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:26.380
the battery will be behind the pilot,

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:27.530
the pilot goes there.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.210
And it's a design by the
designer Sophie Horne,

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:31.410
our region designer.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.350
It looks like a fighter jet.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:34.660
It looks like a fighter jet

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.160
combined with the X wing from Star Wars,

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:38.600
combined with many.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:40.740
It's science fiction in many ways.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:41.728
How fast?

00:13:41.728 --> 00:13:42.863
60 knots.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:45.970
Yeah, they go fast.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.140
Now the real work begins, right?

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.310
Yeah, now the real work begins.

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:51.120
Cities, sponsors, build the calendar,

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:54.530
and start making everything
real so in two years,

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.023
or less than two years, a year and a half

00:13:56.023 --> 00:13:57.563
we hit the ground running.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:00.260
In the meantime,

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:02.910
there's the matter of the
upcoming season of Formula E.

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.480
Alejandro will spend a lot of time

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.280
thinking about sponsors and teams

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.750
and across those teams,

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:10.300
they'll be thinking about the
next generation of technology

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.940
in their cars, known as Gen 3.

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:14.852
There's a lot of excitement
around what that could mean

00:14:14.852 --> 00:14:17.960
on the course and back in our garages.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.950
Gen 3, we will reduce
the weight of the car,

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:23.070
something like, 60 kilo.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:24.790
The biggest improvement is the fact

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:27.421
that in the very beginning
of the Formula E car

00:14:27.421 --> 00:14:32.421
we used two battery per
race for 45 minutes.

00:14:32.448 --> 00:14:35.640
Next a year, in the end of 2022,

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.013
we will use only one car, one battery.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.520
A lighter car with one less battery

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:45.130
means the car overall will have
a smaller carbon footprint.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:48.400
The battery is also expected
to have a faster charge time.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.700
That means it won't require
a battery swap mid-race.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.072
It also means all of us

00:14:53.072 --> 00:14:55.801
could spend less time charging EVs

00:14:55.801 --> 00:14:57.533
and more time on the road.

00:15:01.804 --> 00:15:04.100
Then of course came the
big existential questions

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:06.270
around the future of cars, racecars,

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:09.860
and naturally Formula One and Formula E.

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:12.060
Alejandro's vision is crystal clear,

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.130
someday they will be one.

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.992
I see a convergence at some point

00:15:15.992 --> 00:15:16.913
within Formula One and Formula E

00:15:16.913 --> 00:15:19.990
because Formula One is
gonna lose its industry.

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:21.270
There's not going to
be more combustion cars

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.880
sold in the UK in 2030

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:26.250
so what's the point of a
combustion race in the UK in 2030,

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.260
if you cannot buy combustion cars?

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.225
So eventually, Formula One

00:15:29.225 --> 00:15:33.040
is going to have to do something electric.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.240
And the only way to do it is with us,

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:35.661
cause we have an exclusive license

00:15:35.661 --> 00:15:39.283
from the international
federation until 2039.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:44.000
For now, the circuits exist
in something like parallel,

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.550
with the much younger Formula
E gaining some ground,

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.210
if only because it's in tune

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.890
with the broader global
move to sustainability

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:53.500
and the stated goal of
most major automakers,

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.240
to ditch internal combustion engines.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.363
People perceive motorsport
really glamorous

00:15:58.363 --> 00:16:01.319
and stuff out there, but
reality, trust me is just,

00:16:01.319 --> 00:16:03.310
we are cleaning up a lot of stuff.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:05.500
I feel it's not a job, it's a mission

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.650
and I'm not yet close
to even finishing it.

